WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.060
- I actually was a huge super fan

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.330
when you were on American Idol.

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:05.493
I still am a fan.

00:00:06.832 --> 00:00:08.480
(applause)

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.760
- I did not know this.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.980
- I know I'm not alone;
it's the most obvious thing.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.623
Everybody was obsessed with
you and continues to be.

00:00:15.904 --> 00:00:18.680
But I was supposed to go to the finale

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.733
and I had tickets and I was so excited

00:00:20.733 --> 00:00:23.340
and I was working on that show 24

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.110
and I got a call time that went too late

00:00:26.110 --> 00:00:28.020
and I missed it and I'm still devastated.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.550
- We hate 24 for that; I'm just kidding.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.230
I love 24; I'm just kidding.

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:33.880
- But yeah, so anyway
- Oh man

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.708
- But now look it's like I make up for it.

00:00:35.708 --> 00:00:36.920
- You didn't miss anything.

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:37.753
I just looked like a total boob and cried.

00:00:37.753 --> 00:00:41.168
It was so dumb, I cried,
and they wanted me to sing.

00:00:41.168 --> 00:00:42.686
- I cried too; I watched I crying.

00:00:42.686 --> 00:00:44.317
I was like, she won!

00:00:44.317 --> 00:00:45.420
- I was literally, you know
why I was crying so hard?

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:47.290
Yes, dreams were being
made, but also I was like,

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:50.688
I never have to serve a
drink to a drunk guy again.

00:00:50.688 --> 00:00:53.107
(cheering)

00:00:53.107 --> 00:00:54.730
- Victory.

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:58.050
- You left, doing The Talk, after 10 years

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.400
of doing The Talk, like how was it?

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.270
You just recently went back, how was it?

00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:02.720
- It felt like home, you know,

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.960
when you go back to something
you've been at for so long.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.128
And I was so excited to
go back and see everybody

00:01:08.128 --> 00:01:12.070
and I actually felt more
sad in a way leaving,

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.770
cause it went so fast.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:15.280
Like I was just there for a couple hours.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:16.990
In my mind, I had built up like,

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:18.630
I'm going back! I'm going
back! I'm going back!

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.888
And then I was like, oh it's over.

00:01:20.888 --> 00:01:22.780
- Oh my gosh, it must
have been a trip, though.

00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:24.090
That's a long time to be on a show,

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:25.770
like to create that family.

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:27.560
- It's a long time, it's a long time.

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:31.296
And I'll just keep finding
excuses to go back.

00:01:31.296 --> 00:01:32.568
(applause)

00:01:32.568 --> 00:01:34.296
- I love the group though,
it's a cool group of women.

00:01:34.296 --> 00:01:36.000
- It's a nice group.
- Yeah, I agree.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.816
So what is it like
filming The Conners now,

00:01:38.816 --> 00:01:40.427
is it like 30 years

00:01:40.427 --> 00:01:41.790
after it was on?
- Yeah

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.550
- Cause I grew up with you.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:45.420
I can't believe I'm sitting next to you.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.976
Like I always get freaked out

00:01:46.976 --> 00:01:48.416
(cheering)

00:01:48.416 --> 00:01:50.810
because it's those people that were

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:53.317
constantly in your life like everyday.

00:01:53.317 --> 00:01:55.666
Like those kind of stars that always

00:01:55.666 --> 00:01:58.440
I get star struck with because I'm like,

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:00.630
wait, I was with you like everyday,

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.867
like when you grew up on
TV, like I was growing up.

00:02:02.867 --> 00:02:03.700
- Yeah I feel that with people.

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:05.620
You grow up with them
and it feels so familiar.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:07.546
- Not in a stalker way.

00:02:07.546 --> 00:02:08.555
(laughing)

00:02:08.555 --> 00:02:10.656
Like in a very safe way, yeah.

00:02:10.656 --> 00:02:13.488
- It's incredible for me
too to be with these people

00:02:13.488 --> 00:02:16.210
that I've known my whole life

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:19.600
and have this history with
and do these scenes together

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.670
that have so much built into them.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.867
- It must be an amazing thing
to be a part of something

00:02:24.867 --> 00:02:26.936
that was so rare.

00:02:26.936 --> 00:02:30.010
Like I feel like Rosanne,
like Friends, MASH,

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:31.960
I think there's these shows
that kind of stick out in time.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.700
There's others I'm
forgetting, but I just mean

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:36.720
that the cast is so perfect,
the chemistry is so perfect.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.530
Whatever goes into play, is just perfect.

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:39.860
And I love that like 30 years later

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:40.693
ya'll are doing it again.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:42.608
And you're now in your
second season, right?

00:02:42.608 --> 00:02:43.667
(cheering)

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:45.027
- Yeah
- It's amazing.

00:02:45.027 --> 00:02:46.888
- It's lucky, it's like you can't,

00:02:46.888 --> 00:02:51.456
you just never know when you
put a group of people together

00:02:51.456 --> 00:02:52.873
how it's going to work,

00:02:53.726 --> 00:02:56.610
and part of it is luck
that you have the chemistry

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.000
and the relationships, yeah.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.490
- And just to be a kid in Hollywood

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:00.820
that must have been hard
growing up on the show,

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:02.680
so it's good you had, it was
like a family environment.

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:04.283
That's kinda cool that you had that.

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:05.116
- Yeah, very cool.

00:03:05.116 --> 00:03:05.949
- So it's fun, you're doing it again.

00:03:05.949 --> 00:03:07.615
You're doing second season,

00:03:07.615 --> 00:03:08.448
and you're also executive producer, right?

00:03:08.448 --> 00:03:09.550
- I am.
- So you're acting,

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:11.523
you're executive producer, you're a mom.

00:03:11.523 --> 00:03:13.175
Do you want another job, or?

00:03:13.175 --> 00:03:14.110
(applause)

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:18.095
- It's funny because I left The Talk

00:03:18.095 --> 00:03:19.690
so I would have a little more time

00:03:19.690 --> 00:03:22.300
and then this morning I had a few hours

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:25.201
because I was coming here so my work day

00:03:25.201 --> 00:03:28.670
got pushed later and I literally
didn't know what to do.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:29.950
I was like, I need another job.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.660
- There's no call time,
there's no schedule.

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:33.060
- Yeah.
- I panic.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:34.390
Like 'cause I'm so busy all the time.

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:36.100
I'm with you; it's like
wait nobody is telling me

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:39.070
when to eat or like what to wear or, yeah.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.690
- I function better when I have structure.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:43.160
- But you have more time
for your family though

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.430
now that you're not doing
that and you're just

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.932
doing The Conners right now, right?

00:03:45.932 --> 00:03:47.633
- I do and I get to pick
up my kids sometimes

00:03:47.633 --> 00:03:49.532
or take them to school.

00:03:49.532 --> 00:03:51.330
- Do they come on set ever?

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.610
- They do come on set; they
say they're coming to see me,

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:57.023
but I have a lot of
evidence to the contrary.

00:03:57.023 --> 00:03:57.856
(laughing)

00:03:57.856 --> 00:03:59.810
So they'll come when I do The Conners

00:03:59.810 --> 00:04:02.230
and they'll run around
with all the other kids

00:04:02.230 --> 00:04:03.670
and they say they're watching the show.

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:05.690
And then when I ask,
they have like no idea

00:04:05.690 --> 00:04:07.420
what the plot was.
- Good.

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:08.990
- And then when I did The Talk,

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:11.260
they'd always say like, oh well what are

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.180
the giveaways today?

00:04:13.180 --> 00:04:14.745
- What are the giveaways?

00:04:14.745 --> 00:04:16.141
- And I was like, aren't
you going to come see me?

00:04:16.141 --> 00:04:17.545
They're like no, no, no
we're coming to see you.

00:04:17.545 --> 00:04:18.620
And then all of a sudden,

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:19.843
- But gimme your swag.
- Right

00:04:19.843 --> 00:04:21.214
Then I go into like one of my kid's rooms

00:04:21.214 --> 00:04:23.243
and there's like a new
TV and vacuum cleaner.

00:04:23.243 --> 00:04:24.643
(laughing)

00:04:24.643 --> 00:04:25.910
I'm like, you can't keep that.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.152
- I mean points for getting it!

00:04:28.152 --> 00:04:29.493
I mean that's, they're
going to run a company.

00:04:29.493 --> 00:04:31.990
- They like order it and
everything and suddenly

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:34.352
there's like 14 blenders
in my living room.

00:04:34.352 --> 00:04:36.120
(laughing)

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.690
- That's awesome, my kids do that,

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.560
we all have kids at The
Voice and there's like

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.350
a little compound there
and they always say

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:42.720
they're coming for me
but really they're coming

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.860
for the sugar, the
catering, and the children.

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:46.960
They don't even care that I'm there.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:49.970
- Food is a big, the
food is a big attraction.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:51.942
- God, what is it, yeah
I'm sure it's the food.

00:04:51.942 --> 00:04:54.294
- Well and my food at my
house is like no fun, so.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:56.240
- They don't like me either, weekends,

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.710
I give them weekends, they hate me.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.480
I don't care; I'm like
Ghost of Christmas Future.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:02.313
You don't want to have to work.

00:05:02.313 --> 00:05:05.553
I'm trying to help you!
I'm trying to help you!

